INSTRUCTIONS
Create a simple game using pre-defined functions such as Random, and Sqrt.  

Description

Create a modified Battleship game.  Your job is to "Hide" a submarine in a 10x10 grid.  You will then allow the user to guess where to drop the missile. The program will report the distance between the submarine x and y coordinate, and the user's x and y guess.  The user will guess again until they find the submarine or run out of missiles.  They have 10 missiles to try to hit the submarine, otherwise, the submarine gets away.  

Create a random number for the x and y coordinates of the submarine between 1 and 10.

Allow the program to repeat until the user hits the submarine or they are out of missiles

Allow the user to guess the coordinate

Calculate the Euclidean distance between their guess and the coordinates of the submarine.

Report that they have a Miss and show the distance, Hit and end the game, or that the submarine got away and end the game.

Calculate distance information.Links to an external site.

 

